    "e55bd6e87fdadcd736f37072": {
      "original": "A prototype turning Pison Watch data into timely advice, through iMessage.",
      "text": "",
      "size": 17
    },
    "a668ce60ba9b4a72fb617285": {
      "original": "Pison measures neural and physiological signals. I explored the next step: helping people act on them.",
      "text": "Pison is a startup that specializes in neural data collection. Its watch uses electroneurography to detect electrical signals traveling from the brain through the nerves to the muscles.                               In this project, Pison invited my team to develop new AI features for its existing products.",
      "size": 17
    },
    "3d291417a86936dcecf54ea2": {
      "original": "About Pison",
      "text": "More about Pison",
      "size": null
    },
    "830629a1d0bbb1b2d9aa2e63": {
      "original": "The opportunity",
      "text": "Background",
      "size": 17
    },
    "3f56f52cdbc29e129bf961db": {
      "original": "The opportunity",
      "text": "",
      "size": null
    },
    "ac135e43b8834469d53b0db8": {
      "original": "Through user interviews and market research, we found that Pison was already collecting a wealth of physiological and neural data on an ongoing basis. For users, the real gap was between seeing the data and knowing how to act on it. They could track more and more metrics, yet still struggled to understand what a change meant or what to do about it in the moment.",
      "text": "Through user interviews and market research, we found that Pison was already collecting a wealth of physiological and neural data on an ongoing basis. For users, the real gap was between seeing the data and knowing how to act on it. They could track more and more metrics, yet still struggled to understand what a change meant or what to do about it in the moment.",
